KNOWNBUG
main.cpp
--cpp11 --object-bits 12 --unwind 5 --no-unwinding-assertions
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
Invariant violation: std::less<std::_V2::error_category>::~less
--
Was CORE.  Downgraded when the is_constructible empty-pack fix
(cpp11_is_constructible_empty_pack) corrected __is_constructible<T> with an
empty argument pack: is_constructible<std::less<std::error_category>> now
correctly evaluates true, which enables a libstdc++ deduction path CBMC did not
previously reach.  That path drives cpp_typecheck_resolvet::guess_template_args
into deep recursion on std::error_category's (polymorphic, self-referential)
type graph.  A depth guard now prevents the resulting stack overflow (the crash
this test used to guard against), but the deduction is left incomplete, so the
regex verification no longer reaches VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL.  Flip back to CORE
once guess_template_args handles the std::error_category type cycle (cycle
detection rather than a depth cutoff) so the deduction completes.
